                <head>Chapter V.—Transitory provisions (Art. 375)</head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Article</hi> 375.</p>
                <p>Germany shall carry out the instructions given her, in regard to transport, by an
                    authorised body acting on behalf of the Allied and Associated Powers: <list>
                        <label>(1)</label>
                        <item>For the carriage of troops under the provisions of the present Treaty,
                            and of material, ammunition and supplies for army use;</item>
                        <label>(2)</label>
                        <item>As a temporary measure, for the transportation of supplies for certain
                            regions, as well as for the restoration, as rapidly as possible, of the
                            normal conditions of transport, and for the organisation of postal and
                            telegraphic services.</item>
                    </list></p>
            </div>
